  "title": "AI generated 3D scenes",
  "date": "2026-11-06T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "AI generated 3D scenes\n\nThis is the post continue AI generated GLBs.\n\nBlender generate one scene\n\nLast post, I mentioned ZZ是画渣-不用GPT-6！本地模型操作Blender建模教程，0元复刻GPT-6的相同效果？\n\nblender one scene\n\nThis tutorial mentioned the importance of Agent.md. At first, generate the Agent.md with the following prompt.\n\nThen all the assets will have one blender file each, and there is a main.blender to inlude all of them. This result looks fine at a glance. But many details need to adjust either by the agent or manually.\n\nConcept picture first\n\n西高君-AI生成3D游戏场景/Codex+Blender三维模型方法/HD-2D·原来如此简单！. This tutorial firstly generate a concept pic, then make the 3d assets one by one and evetually assemble them in the godot engine.\n\nConcept picture\n\nFirst, make the concept picture's prompt.\n\nThen, use the returned prompt with shome research picture to generate the wished picture.\n\ngenerated image\n\nThe first generated image will be smaller, you need to ask agent to move the camera back, zoom the scene to 4 times or 5 times.\n\nSplit the concept into prompts\n\nUse the following to extract concept picture into prompts. This does not need high end model, Haiku 5.5 can also done the job.\n\nWhat I learned from this, is that I can extract further buildings into one picture. This reminds me that I can solve the Tallinn city model problem I used to struggle, because there were too many meshes in the scene.\n\nGenerate the models\n\nThis needs OpenAI's skill ImageGen to be prepared. However, I fogot that, and used Opus 5.5. The result was even better than the tutorial one...\n\nGenerate Godot Templates\n\nThis is make sure all the assets imported later will be debuggable.\n\nImport the assets\n\nParicles\n\nThe particles should also include debug options\n\nLight\n\nThe light is quite important, beside adjust the sun. The environment also has to be adjusted. There are some shaders included in the tutorial. However, I did not find them very needed. The original one is already good enough.\n\nThen add the character, the game is ready.\n\nresult\n\nThreejs build\n\nLater, I asked agents to refactor the two projects into threejs. Still, some details were lost, like no particles. But the token usage is becoming acceptable now.\n\nConclusion\n\nSurprisingly, these two projects only cost me 70% of 5h credits. That means, I do not need to burnout in coding or saving tokens anymore.",
